  "which_town": {
    "answer": "rift_dig_camp",
    "why": "'The Rift mining town' is the Rift dig camp on the west spur (data/towns.json rift_dig_camp, data/placements.json settlements.rift_dig_camp; docs/world-building/DEEP_CITY.md section 6 'the dig camp as a mining town'; EXP-035 row 19 'The Rift's mining town (the dig camp) is far too small'). It is not mining_town, which is the Craters' mining town in the east cones (x6520-6746 z5603-5829): the owner's notes 'can't have wood houses' and 'needs mine rails, ore piles, tons of theatrics' are that town's (EXP-035 rows 23-24, built by tools/mining_works.py), and 'the southern part of rift ... town and mega stone mine' is the gulch design in docs/world-building/SOUTHERN_RIFT.md."
  },
  "disagreements": [
    "SOUTHERN_RIFT.md puts the mega stone mine in the gulch (the south-east branch, x4039-4454 z4513-4958) behind an 8-badge gate at the end of the game. The owner's request of 2026-09-27 puts the mega stone mines and caves in the dig camp's spur, visible early and gated around badge five or six. This file follows the owner: the mine's design (a seam, an adit hall, galleries with crystal faces, dead-end Mega chambers, a Heart, guardian modes) is SOUTHERN_RIFT.md section 4's, sited in the west spur. The gulch mine is not built and not cancelled.",
    "RIFT_ZONES.md makes the west spur Z1, opened at 2 badges, and data/spawns.json rift_west_spur spawns at 56-58: the band is wrong for a zone opened at 2 badges and for galleries opened at 5 (DEEP_CITY.md section 6 says so too). Not changed here: trainer-balance-designer's.",
    "The placement plan says the camp is strung 'between walls twenty blocks high'. On the canonical heightmap the spur here is a shallow bowl: floor y87, rising about one block in five to y113-115 at z3080 (north) and y104 at z3400 (south). The quarries and worked faces are cut into those slopes to make the walls a mining town needs."
  ],
  "design": [
    "docs/world-building/SOUTHERN_RIFT.md section 4 (the mine, the guardian modes, crystal faces, rewards per player)",
    "docs/world-building/DEEP_CITY.md section 6 (the dig camp as a mining town: stone and copper, no timber; ore piles from blocks that decide nothing; carts)",
    "docs/research/notes/wild-mega-pokemon.md and experiments/EXP-036-wild-mega/README.md (a wild Mega is achievable)",
    "docs/mechanics/RIFT_ZONES.md section 4 (the zone check pattern)"
