  "geometry": {
    "feet": "every y in a path, room box, pocket or chamber is the FEET level: the first air block above the floor. A cut's `floor` is the solid floor block itself (as tools/ground.py's ground is).",
    "tube": "each segment P0->P1 is sampled at n = ceil(4 * horizontal length) + 1 evenly spaced points (one point for a zero-length segment); a point stamps the square of columns within r (Chebyshev) of (floor(x+0.5), floor(z+0.5)), from feet = floor(y+0.5) up `height` blocks",
    "room": "the box, inclusive, feet y0 to top y1",
    "shaft": "the columns within r (Chebyshev) of the centre, from from_y up to one under the ground, where an iron grate caps it",
    "pocket": "columns with dx2+dz2 <= (r+0.5)^2 round the centre; feet to feet+r+1 where dx2+dz2 <= (r-0.5)^2, else feet to feet+r",
    "chamber": "columns with d = hypot(dx, dz) <= r+0.5; feet to feet + max(3, floor((height-1) * sqrt(1 - (d/(r+0.5))^2) + 0.5))",
    "cut": "each column of the rect gets a floor block y_f = floor + rise * level, level = max(0, levels-1 - e // run), e its distance in columns to the nearest benched side (hillside: the sides listed; pit: all four; no benches: level 0); a pit's ramp sets y_f to floor(floor + (z1-z)/(z1-z0) * (top-floor) + 0.5) inside its x/z range (a causeway down through the benches). Where the ground is above y_f the column is cut from y_f+1 to ground+6.",
    "shell": "every cell within 2 (a 5x5x5 cube) of the envelope that is not carved and is at or under the ground is written as rock, so the cut and carved spaces are bounded only by blocks this build writes",
    "roughness": "gated tubes, pockets and chambers only: an envelope cell on the envelope's edge, 3 or more above its column's floor, is left as rock with probability 0.3 (deterministic hash); nothing is ever carved outside the envelope"
  }
}
